&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;ABOUT US&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;E-commerce got real-time data infrastructure decades ago. Physical stores still have not. RADAR is changing that.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;RADAR is building the data infrastructure layer for the physical world, starting with retail. Our hardware-enabled SaaS platform uses proprietary overhead sensors, software, and AI-powered analytics to locate every product in a store, continuously, down to the fixture. We are&amp;nbsp;deployed across 1,400+ stores with retailers including American Eagle Outfitters and Old Navy, processing tens of billions of real-world events every day, delivering 99%+ accuracy in complex, noisy environments - at fleet scale.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;RADAR is one of the best-funded companies in retail technology, backed by a recent Series B financing at a $1 billion valuation. Inventory accuracy is only the beginning. We believe RADAR can become foundational infrastructure for the physical economy, powering new AI-driven commerce experiences across retail and beyond.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Join us if you want to work on a large, unsolved, technically challenging problem with an ambitious team building category-defining technology.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;OUR VALUES&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mission-Driven: We&#39;re transforming retail with cutting-edge technology and building something that truly matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative Team: We thrive on curiosity, shared goals, and solving complex problems together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High Impact: You’ll make meaningful contributions from day one and help shape the future of our product and company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear Communication: We value honesty, humility, and respectful dialogue—everyone’s voice matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balanced Lives: We work hard, but not at the expense of well-being. We respect time, boundaries, and life outside of work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diverse Perspectives: We believe better ideas come from diverse backgrounds, experiences, and viewpoints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Empathy-Driven Design: We build with deep respect for our end users, listening closely to their feedback and needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE JOB&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an Accounting Manager who doesn’t just keep the books clean - they build the systems, processes, and controls that scale with the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you’ll own the core accounting engine at RADAR: driving a fast, accurate month-end close, leveling up our financial infrastructure, and helping us get audit-ready for the first time. You’ll be at the center of how money moves through the company - from revenue and inventory to payments, systems, and reporting - with real influence on how we operate as we grow.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on leadership role for someone who likes to roll up their sleeves, spot inefficiencies, and turn “how it’s always been done” into something better. You’ll partner across the company, shape processes from the ground up, and help build a modern, scalable accounting function powered by tools like NetSuite, Bill.com, Brex, Rippling, and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and drive the month-end close - ensuring speed, accuracy, and zero surprises&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and deliver clear, insightful financial reporting for leadership, including variance analysis and key business drivers and actionable insights for the business to improve operations and financial performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Raise the bar on accounting quality, controls, and GAAP compliance across the board&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply technical accounting expertise (ASC 606, ASC 842, etc.) to real-world business decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage Procure-to-Pay workflows end-to-end, ensuring clean data, strong controls, and smooth operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and work through our first external audit with us&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, document, and continuously improve accounting policies, processes, and internal controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own inventory accounting across raw materials, WIP, finished goods, and in-transit inventory for our integrated hardware / software platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with external tax advisors and support income tax preparation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support international expansion and the complexities that come with it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with the NetSuite team to stabilize, optimize, and expand our ERP capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, mentor, and elevate the accounting team - setting a high bar for quality and ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate cross-functionally with teams across Procurement, Growth, Operations, HR, Legal, Tax, IT, and Strategic Finance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;ABOUT YOU&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, or related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5–8+ years of progressive accounting experience, ideally in a high-growth tech environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong command of US GAAP, month-end close, and operational accounting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with NetSuite or a similar modern ERP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience reviewing work and guiding others to high-quality output&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You take ownership, move fast, and don’t wait to be told what to fix&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Bill.com, Brex, Sphere, Rippling, and/or NetSuite&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in public accounting or audit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inventory or cost accounting experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to international expansion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CPA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in lean teams or startup environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL DO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In your first 30 days, you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Get up to speed on RADAR’s business, tech, and financial architecture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn our systems (NetSuite, Bill.com, Brex, Rippling, etc.) and current workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dive into the close process, reconciliations, and reporting structure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In your first 60 days, you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take ownership of key parts of the close and begin reviewing work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify gaps, risks, and inefficiencies across close, inventory, and reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Start tightening documentation, controls, and SOPs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In your first 90 days, you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully own the close process and deliver it with confidence and consistency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ship meaningful improvements to inventory and reporting workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish strong review standards and elevate team output&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver measurable gains in data quality, controls, and reporting reliability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;At RADAR, your base pay is one part of your total compensation package. The expected base salary range for this position is $120,000-165,000. Individual pay is determined by work location and additional factors,&amp;nbsp; including job-related skills, experience and relevant education or training.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;You will also be eligible to receive other benefits including: equity, comprehensive medical and dental coverage, life and disability benefits, 401k plan,&amp;nbsp; flexible time off, and paid parental leave. The pay range listed for this position is a good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible base compensation at the time of posting.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Research has shown that women &amp;amp; underrepresented minorities are more likely to read lists of requirements and consider themselves unqualified if they don&#39;t meet every single one. This list represents what we&#39;re ideally looking for, but everyone has unique strengths &amp;amp; weaknesses, and we hire for strength &amp;amp; potential, not lack of weakness.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;ABOUT US&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;E-commerce got real-time data infrastructure decades ago. Physical stores still have not. RADAR is changing that.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;RADAR is building the data infrastructure layer for the physical world, starting with retail. Our hardware-enabled SaaS platform uses proprietary overhead sensors, software, and AI-powered analytics to locate every product in a store, continuously, down to the fixture. We are&amp;nbsp;deployed across 1,400+ stores with retailers including American Eagle Outfitters and Old Navy, processing tens of billions of real-world events every day, delivering 99%+ accuracy in complex, noisy environments - at fleet scale.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;RADAR is one of the best-funded companies in retail technology, backed by a recent Series B financing at a $1 billion valuation. Inventory accuracy is only the beginning. We believe RADAR can become foundational infrastructure for the physical economy, powering new AI-driven commerce experiences across retail and beyond.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Join us if you want to work on a large, unsolved, technically challenging problem with an ambitious team building category-defining technology.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;OUR VALUES&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mission-Driven: We&#39;re transforming retail with cutting-edge technology and building something that truly matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative Team: We thrive on curiosity, shared goals, and solving complex problems together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High Impact: You’ll make meaningful contributions from day one and help shape the future of our product and company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear Communication: We value honesty, humility, and respectful dialogue—everyone’s voice matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balanced Lives: We work hard, but not at the expense of well-being. We respect time, boundaries, and life outside of work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diverse Perspectives: We believe better ideas come from diverse backgrounds, experiences, and viewpoints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Empathy-Driven Design: We build with deep respect for our end users, listening closely to their feedback and needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE JOB&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Deployment Associate at Radar plays a critical role in the successful deployment of RADAR technology in retail stores. A successful candidate will possess a combination of technical skills, attention to detail, and the ability to work effectively as part of a team.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deployment Associates at Radar are responsible for the end-to-end deployment lifecycle of a store portfolio within their region. This isn’t a handoff role. You’ll oversee your stores from start to finish: from coordinating with external partners before a technician sets foot on site, to ensuring the installations are completed on schedule, and completing a final QA assessment and sign-off.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Deployment Operations:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pre-Installation Coordination:&lt;/strong&gt; Communicate with external partners and stakeholders to ensure alignment on tasks, timelines, and requirements for upcoming installations. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Project Execution:&lt;/strong&gt; Collaborate with the Deployment Lead, as well as Operations and Support teams, to ensure stores are completed efficiently and in line with Radar standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Feedback Loop:&lt;/strong&gt; Serve as an invaluable resource to field crews, providing input and feedback on deployment procedures to improve our workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Quality Assurance:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Conduct Checks:&lt;/strong&gt; Perform quality checks on installations, both remotely and in-person, to confirm they meet Radar’s standards.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Document Findings:&lt;/strong&gt; Keep detailed records of any issues encountered and track them through resolution.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process Adherence:&lt;/strong&gt; Ensure all deployment activities closely follow established procedures and guidelines.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Training and Development:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Participate in &lt;/strong&gt;training sessions to deepen understanding of RADAR technology and deployment procedures.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skill Development:&lt;/strong&gt; Continuously develop technical skills through hands-on experience and training.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Knowledge Sharing:&lt;/strong&gt; Assist in training new Deployment Associates, vendor partners, and other team members involved in the deployment process by sharing knowledge and best practices.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Documentation: &lt;/strong&gt;Contribute to documenting procedures and guidelines, and assist with ongoing revisions and improvements to the documentation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Safety and Compliance:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Follow Safety Protocols:&lt;/strong&gt; Adhere to all safety standards and protocols during installations to ensure a safe working environment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance Checks:&lt;/strong&gt; Ensure all installations comply with company policies and regulatory requirements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Incident Reporting:&lt;/strong&gt; Report any safety incidents or compliance issues to the Deployment Lead immediately.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;ABOUT YOU&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have some experience in technology deployment or a related field, preferably within retail environments.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a basic understanding of hardware installations and technical troubleshooting.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have strong attention to detail and commitment to quality.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are able to work well in a team and follow directions from senior team members.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have good communication skills, both verbal and written.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are willing to learn and adapt to new technologies and procedures.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are able to multitask and work in a dynamic environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have previous experience with RFID technology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are willing to work weekends, nights, and holidays, as needed.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL DO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In your first 30 days, you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn about Radar&#39;s mission, history, and technology.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meet key team members and understand their roles.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in training sessions on RADAR technology and deployment procedures.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in a few deployment projects under the guidance of senior team members.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In your first 60 days, you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take a more active role in deployment projects, handling installation tasks independently.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continue learning from senior team members and asking questions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Start identifying areas for personal improvement and seek feedback from the Deployment Operations Leads and peers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate with team members to walk through resolutions and manage escalations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In your first 90 days, you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Begin taking ownership of your assigned store portfolio by completing tasks, managing quality assurance, and ensuring installations meet Radar’s standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in team meetings and contribute ideas for improving deployment processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to improving deployment processes and documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate personal progress and set goals for the future with input from the Deployment Operations Leads.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;At RADAR, your base pay is one part of your total compensation package. The expected base salary range for this position is $75,000-$100,000. Individual pay is determined by work location and additional factors,&amp;nbsp; including job-related skills, experience and relevant education or training.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;You will also be eligible to receive other benefits including: equity, comprehensive medical and dental coverage, life and disability benefits, 401k plan,&amp;nbsp; flexible time off, and paid parental leave. The pay range listed for this position is a good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible base compensation at the time of posting.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Research has shown that women &amp;amp; underrepresented minorities are more likely to read lists of requirements and consider themselves unqualified if they don&#39;t meet every single one. This list represents what we&#39;re ideally looking for, but everyone has unique strengths &amp;amp; weaknesses, and we hire for strength &amp;amp; potential, not lack of weakness.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;ABOUT US&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;E-commerce got real-time data infrastructure decades ago. Physical stores still have not. RADAR is changing that.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;RADAR is building the data infrastructure layer for the physical world, starting with retail. Our hardware-enabled SaaS platform uses proprietary overhead sensors, software, and AI-powered analytics to locate every product in a store, continuously, down to the fixture. We are&amp;nbsp;deployed across 1,400+ stores with retailers including American Eagle Outfitters and Old Navy, processing tens of billions of real-world events every day, delivering 99%+ accuracy in complex, noisy environments - at fleet scale.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;RADAR is one of the best-funded companies in retail technology, backed by a recent Series B financing at a $1 billion valuation. Inventory accuracy is only the beginning. We believe RADAR can become foundational infrastructure for the physical economy, powering new AI-driven commerce experiences across retail and beyond.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Join us if you want to work on a large, unsolved, technically challenging problem with an ambitious team building category-defining technology.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;OUR VALUES&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mission-Driven: We&#39;re transforming retail with cutting-edge technology and building something that truly matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative Team: We thrive on curiosity, shared goals, and solving complex problems together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High Impact: You’ll make meaningful contributions from day one and help shape the future of our product and company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear Communication: We value honesty, humility, and respectful dialogue—everyone’s voice matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balanced Lives: We work hard, but not at the expense of well-being. We respect time, boundaries, and life outside of work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diverse Perspectives: We believe better ideas come from diverse backgrounds, experiences, and viewpoints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Empathy-Driven Design: We build with deep respect for our end users, listening closely to their feedback and needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE JOB&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Director, Business Development to own and grow RADAR&#39;s external relationships with retail brands and drive targets through the commercial pipeline — from first conversation to signed partnership. This is a quota-carrying, revenue-facing role at the center of RADAR&#39;s next stage of growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll be the face of RADAR to VP- and C-level stakeholders across merchandising, store operations, supply chain, and IT at multi-national apparel brands, department stores, and big-box retailers. You&#39;ll build and manage a pipeline of qualified opportunities, run a consultative and technically credible sales process, and work cross-functionally with Product, Engineering, Marketing, Customer Experience and Deployment Operations to turn interest into signed, deployed customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role requires equal parts hunter instinct and relationship-building discipline — someone who can open doors at the executive level, translate a technical, hardware-enabled platform into a business case retailers act on, and manage a multi-stakeholder, multi-month sales cycle without losing momentum.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Pipeline Ownership&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end business development pipeline for a defined set of target retail accounts, from prospecting and qualification through to signed contract.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain accurate pipeline reporting and forecasting, using CRM discipline to keep stage, next steps, and close timing current for leadership visibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively move targets through the pipeline, identifying and clearing the blockers that stall enterprise retail deals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;External Relationships &amp;amp; Partnerships&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and own senior-level relationships with retail executives across merchandising, store operations, supply chain, loss prevention, and IT.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as RADAR&#39;s primary external point of contact for prospective retail partners throughout the sales cycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent RADAR at industry events, conferences, and retailer forums to build market presence and generate new relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Deal Strategy &amp;amp; Execution&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the commercial narrative for each opportunity: translate RADAR&#39;s hardware-enabled platform into a clear, retailer-specific business case tied to inventory accuracy, labor efficiency, and fulfillment performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Structure and negotiate commercial terms, partnering with Legal and Finance to close agreements that work for both RADAR and the retailer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate proof-of-concept and pilot store engagements alongside Engineering and Deployment Operations to prove value ahead of full rollout.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product and Marketing to bring retailer feedback and market intelligence back into RADAR&#39;s roadmap and positioning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Deployment Operations and Customer Experience to ensure a smooth handoff from signed deal to live store rollout.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide leadership with regular visibility into pipeline health, deal risk, and market trends across the retail landscape.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Market Intelligence&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track competitive dynamics, retail technology trends, and buying behavior across target verticals to sharpen RADAR&#39;s go-to-market approach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify new verticals, account segments, or partnership models that expand RADAR&#39;s addressable market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;ABOUT YOU&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of business development, enterprise sales, or strategic partnerships experience, with a track record of owning and closing complex, multi-stakeholder, multi-million dollar deals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling into retail — brand, big-box, or department store organizations — with an existing network at the VP/C-level across merchandising, store operations, supply chain, or IT.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to manage a full sales pipeline independently: prospecting, qualification, solution development, negotiation, and close.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort selling a hardware-enabled, technical platform to a non-technical business audience — you can translate complex capability into a business case executives act on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commercial instincts: you know how to structure a deal, negotiate terms, and know when to push and when to slow down.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent executive presence and communication skills, with the ability to build credibility quickly with senior retail stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A builder&#39;s mindset — comfortable operating with limited process, creating your own playbook, and adapting as the business scales.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel to meet prospective and existing retail partners as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling RFID, IoT, computer vision, or other in-store hardware/software solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Existing relationships with retail executives at brands in RADAR&#39;s target segments (apparel, big-box, department stores).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with Engineering or Deployment teams to run pilots and proofs of concept.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with CRM and pipeline management tools (Salesforce, HubSpot, or similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
