&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL DO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In your first 30 days, you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn about Radar&#39;s mission, technology, deployed hardware, and Customer Support organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meet key partners across Customer Support, Engineering, Deployment Operations, Logistics, and other Operations teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn the current Support escalation, field dispatch, RMA, and hardware troubleshooting processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in active field maintenance cases alongside existing team members and field service partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Begin learning common field failure modes and how RADAR validates successful resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In your first 60 days, you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Begin independently owning field maintenance escalations from initial triage through resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate field technicians, customer contacts, replacement hardware, and internal technical resources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide remote troubleshooting guidance to technicians working onsite.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify gaps in existing technician procedures, escalation paths, documentation, and field maintenance workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Begin tracking repeat visits, recurring failure types, field partner performance, and opportunities to improve first-time resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build stronger feedback loops between Customer Support, Field Maintenance, Deployment Operations, and Engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In your first 90 days, you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
