&lt;h4&gt;OUR VALUES&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mission-Driven: We&#39;re transforming retail with cutting-edge technology and building something that truly matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative Team: We thrive on curiosity, shared goals, and solving complex problems together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High Impact: You’ll make meaningful contributions from day one and help shape the future of our product and company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear Communication: We value honesty, humility, and respectful dialogue—everyone’s voice matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balanced Lives: We work hard, but not at the expense of well-being. We respect time, boundaries, and life outside of work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diverse Perspectives: We believe better ideas come from diverse backgrounds, experiences, and viewpoints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Empathy-Driven Design: We build with deep respect for our end users, listening closely to their feedback and needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE JOB&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Software Engineer Manager you will lead the General Platform team, the full stack engineering group responsible for tenant and store onboarding and our core front end RADAR experience. This is a player-coach role leading an established team with full accountability from day one, and shaping how the team scales as our platform and customer base grow.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The best leaders here are strong engineers first. You will be expected to engage deeply with architecture and technical direction, not just manage processes. We move fast, and you know how to hold a high quality bar without sacrificing velocity, along with the judgment to know when to push and when to slow down to get it right.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the General Platform team end to end, including tenant and store onboarding systems and the core front end RADAR experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, mentor, and grow a team of engineers; own performance management, career development, and team culture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set technical direction and support architecture decisions for onboarding and front end platform systems, and champion engineering best practices across the team and with peers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay technically engaged through design reviews, architecture decisions, and code review as a practicing engineer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage agile processes, execution priorities, and on time delivery of high quality solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Product, UX, and cross functional stakeholders to define roadmap, project plans, and requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, communicate, and drive resolution for technical and organizational risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a culture of security, quality, operational accountability, and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support hiring and help grow the broader engineering organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent General Platform in cross functional conversations and act as a strong point of integration across the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;ABOUT YOU&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s or Master&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of software engineering experience, including at least 2 years managing engineering teams of 5 or more direct reports.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to remain technically hands on, contributing to design, architecture, and code review as a practicing engineer, not just an overseer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience owning full stack systems in production, including both backend platform services and front end applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in at least one core language such as Java, Python, C++, or Go, and familiarity with modern front end frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with onboarding, provisioning, or multi tenant platform systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid foundation in systems or cloud architecture, DevOps and SecOps practices, automation, and CI/CD pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, organizational, and people leadership skills, with experience influencing across engineering, product, and design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience working at a startup or high growth company, with firsthand understanding of the pace, ambiguity, and tradeoffs that come with that stage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading a team through a period of significant growth or organizational change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background at a startup or high growth company where you saw both the value of moving fast and the cost of cutting corners on quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience owning a customer facing front end platform alongside backend infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with cloud platforms such as AWS, GCP, or Azure, and container orchestration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or scaling multi tenant SaaS platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for mentoring, technical empowerment, and building an inclusive engineering culture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL DO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In your first 30 days, you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build context on an established, larger team; hold off on making changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meet every direct report 1:1 and begin building trust and rapport.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shadow team rituals across the full General Platform team: standups, planning, retros, design reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Map the systems the team owns: onboarding architecture, front end platform, dependencies, operational health.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meet key cross functional partners across product, design, and peer engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meet peer managers and senior stakeholders to understand how work flows across teams and where friction exists.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify any immediate fires or risks that need attention before deeper learning is complete.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In your first 60 days, you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute meaningfully across both the onboarding systems and the front end platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish a consistent 1:1 cadence and begin individual development conversations across the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively participate in design and architecture discussions spanning onboarding and front end systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clarify team goals, priorities, and near term delivery commitments across the team&#39;s full scope.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify process or quality gaps across the broader team and begin forming a point of view on how to address them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver or unblock at least one meaningful piece of work alongside the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In your first 90 days, you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate with full ownership of General Platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present an initial roadmap or priority framework for General Platform to your manager and stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a clear development plan in place for each direct report.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be actively driving execution across onboarding and front end systems: unblocking the team, removing friction, and holding a high bar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own at least one cross functional initiative or decision end to end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a concrete plan to improve one dimension of team health: quality, velocity, culture, or process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish a clear voice in cross functional conversations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;At RADAR, your base pay is one part of your total compensation package. The expected base salary range for this position is $200,000-$250,000. Individual pay is determined by work location and additional factors,&amp;nbsp; including job-related skills, experience and relevant education or training.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;You will also be eligible to receive other benefits including: equity, comprehensive medical and dental coverage, life and disability benefits, 401k plan,&amp;nbsp; flexible time off, and paid parental leave. The pay range listed for this position is a good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible base compensation at the time of posting.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Research has shown that women &amp;amp; underrepresented minorities are more likely to read lists of requirements and consider themselves unqualified if they don&#39;t meet every single one. This list represents what we&#39;re ideally looking for, but everyone has unique strengths &amp;amp; weaknesses, and we hire for strength &amp;amp; potential, not lack of weakness.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;ABOUT US&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;E-commerce got real-time data infrastructure decades ago. Physical stores still have not. RADAR is changing that.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;RADAR is building the data infrastructure layer for the physical world, starting with retail. Our hardware-enabled SaaS platform uses proprietary overhead sensors, software, and AI-powered analytics to locate every product in a store, continuously, down to the fixture. We are&amp;nbsp;deployed across 1,400+ stores with retailers including American Eagle Outfitters and Old Navy, processing tens of billions of real-world events every day, delivering 99%+ accuracy in complex, noisy environments - at fleet scale.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;RADAR is one of the best-funded companies in retail technology, backed by a recent Series B financing at a $1 billion valuation. Inventory accuracy is only the beginning. We believe RADAR can become foundational infrastructure for the physical economy, powering new AI-driven commerce experiences across retail and beyond.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Join us if you want to work on a large, unsolved, technically challenging problem with an ambitious team building category-defining technology.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;OUR VALUES&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mission-Driven: We&#39;re transforming retail with cutting-edge technology and building something that truly matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative Team: We thrive on curiosity, shared goals, and solving complex problems together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High Impact: You’ll make meaningful contributions from day one and help shape the future of our product and company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear Communication: We value honesty, humility, and respectful dialogue—everyone’s voice matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balanced Lives: We work hard, but not at the expense of well-being. We respect time, boundaries, and life outside of work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diverse Perspectives: We believe better ideas come from diverse backgrounds, experiences, and viewpoints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Empathy-Driven Design: We build with deep respect for our end users, listening closely to their feedback and needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE JOB&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an experienced Staff Software Technical Program Manager to lead the development, delivery, and ongoing operations of fleetwide RFID solutions to retailers worldwide. The ideal candidate will combine technical expertise in software development and test with strong program management skills to drive successful product development and launch.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead programs in software development, data governance, and feature implementation through the entire SWDL, including requirements management, architectural design, proof of concept/proof of experience, engineering pilots, unit testing, scale validation, fleet deployment, and sustaining engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and drive success. Provide clarity and develop detailed execution plans for large, complex, ambiguous software programs. Successfully execute said plans by removing blockers and ensuring the proper sense of urgency while providing cross-functional visibility/reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify interdependencies and bottlenecks, evaluate and optimize workflows, and dig deep when critical issues arise to ensure developers are unblocked and problems are escalated quickly/appropriately&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Look around corners for “what if” scenarios and develop detailed risk mitigation plans where appropriate based on risk level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Switch gears regularly between the high level 10k foot view to detailed microscopic view for critical activities where needed based on audience, communicating information tactfully and effectively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive software releases through rigorous testing and validation activities from unit level to E2E system level to ensure KPIs are met with clear exit criteria. Ensure best practices are met from a quality perspective to enable frequent deployments at scale (CI/CD, stability, additional automations, etc)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage/coordinate production issue RCAs and remediation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate effective ways of working among various cross-functional teams not just within software, but partner teams such as Data Science, Systems Engineering, Product Management, Customer Experience, Deployment Operations, Embedded Systems, and Hardware teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support key customer relationships and expectations management in collaboration with Customer Experience and Product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present regular status updates to executive stakeholders and cross-functional leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage cloud costs and cost reduction initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;ABOUT YOU&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Data Science, or related technical field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in software/infra program management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience as a software engineer, data scientist, or related field&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated expertise in managing the complete software product development cycle&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient with project management tools including Smartsheet, Jira, Confluence, and methodologies including Agile (SAFe), Waterfall, Scrum, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with test plan development and execution for various levels of SW validation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of software development “V” process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, leadership, and interpersonal skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Problem-solving mindset with the ability to navigate technical and organizational challenges in a start-up environment while setting up for long term success as we scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work on-site or hybrid in Seattle, WA (preferred) or Sunnyvale, CA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with RFID and wireless technology&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with retailer supply chain and inventory management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with cloud and backend services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with mobile applications development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with edge compute, shadow controllers, network architectures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with ring based deployments, feature flags, blue/green deployments, and health probes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with regulatory compliance requirements (SOC 1, SOC 2, pen testing)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with containerization (K8s, K3s) and configuration management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with observability platforms and dashboards (New Relic, Grafana, Looker)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with firmware development and hardware/software integration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with internationalization and localization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with writing PRDs and requirements tracking software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Project management training/certification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL DO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In your first 30 days, you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn Radar’s mission, technology stack and core values.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complete onboarding and security compliance training.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarization with ways of working and tooling used, including Jira, Confluence, JPD, BigPicture, Smartsheet, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarization with release workflows, teams, ceremonies, and reporting best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ask lots of questions!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In your first 60 days, you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand in detail the current state of SW infrastructure&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand in detail the H2 ‘26 and 2027 product roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to sprint planning, backlog grooming, and overall Scrum/SAFe model including task and bug management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Start driving execution and delivery of engineering initiatives and reporting out&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gatekeep for the Definition of Ready, Definition of Done, and the SW release strategy for your program(s)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish program ceremonies and reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ask more questions, align teams, ask why, challenge assumptions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In your first 90 days, you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently manage 1-2 programs&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive resolution of critical issues by collaborating with DRIs and XFN teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the SW roadmap strategy and program increment planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively identify and engage with potential downstream risks and opportunities, such as maximizing efficiency and reducing bottlenecks, and escalating when appropriate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to capacity planning and prioritization exercises&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep asking questions and eventually be a thought leader&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
